<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Askia Muhammad's pilgrimage</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1496">1496</a>–<a href="/years/1498">1498</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/askia-muhammad">Askia Muhammad</a>'s pilgrimage was the journey to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> made by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai</a> ruler Askia Muhammad between 1496 and 1498. During it he was recognised by the Abbasid shadow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a> as his representative in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>. The pilgrimage enhanced his Islamic legitimacy and links with the wider Muslim world.</p></div>
